🗂️ Mock Data Structure
To simulate realistic data, we'll use a mock JSON structure inspired by standard insurance modules. Here's an overview of the data schema:
Members: Contains information about individuals registered in the system.
omember_id: Unique identifier for each member.
oname: Full name of the member.
odate_of_birth: Date of birth.
ogender: Gender.
ocontact_info: Contact details, including email and phone number.
oaddress: Residential address.
oregistration_date: Date the member registered.
Contributions: Records of financial contributions made by members.
ocontribution_id: Unique identifier for each contribution.
omember_id: Identifier linking to the contributing member.
oamount: Contribution amount.
odate: Date of contribution.
ostatus: Status of the contribution (e.g., paid, pending).
Benefits: Details of benefits allocated to members.
obenefit_id: Unique identifier for each benefit.
omember_id: Identifier linking to the beneficiary.
otype: Type of benefit (e.g., pension, health).
oamount: Benefit amount.
ostatus: Status of the benefit (e.g., approved, pending).
odate: Date the benefit was allocated.
This structure is designed to align with typical insurance data management systems, facilitating a comprehensive demonstration of the RSSBDMS functionalities.
